00:01:55.706 --> 00:01:57.831
- [Voiceover] Gregory asked,
"If you ever become the CEO

00:01:57.831 --> 00:02:00.269
"of a local Chamber of
a community of 12,000,

00:02:00.269 --> 00:02:01.761
"what would be the first
thing you would do?"

00:02:04.294 --> 00:02:06.944
- If I became the CEO of a
Chamber of Commerce for a

00:02:06.944 --> 00:02:09.184
small group of 12,000 people,

00:02:09.184 --> 00:02:12.145
12,000 members or 12,000 people in a town?

00:02:12.145 --> 00:02:13.039
- [Steve] Community, yeah.

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:18.588
- You know, I'm a very big
fan of scaling the unscalable.

00:02:18.588 --> 00:02:20.793
Right, I talk a lot about engagement,

00:02:20.793 --> 00:02:25.367
one on one engagement, Twitter
videos, depth versus width.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.026
When you're talking about
a town of 12,000 people,

00:02:28.026 --> 00:02:29.872
even if we're answering this incorrectly

00:02:29.872 --> 00:02:32.124
and it's a membership of 12,000,

00:02:32.124 --> 00:02:34.642
it's still a very small number
in the scheme of things.

00:02:34.642 --> 00:02:39.642
So, what I would fundamentally
do is create a infrastructure

00:02:40.087 --> 00:02:43.165
to allow me to connect one by one

00:02:44.235 --> 00:02:46.949
with every single member of the Chamber,

00:02:46.949 --> 00:02:51.511
and even considering if it's
a 12,000 person community

00:02:51.511 --> 00:02:54.576
the thousand to 4,000
people that really care

00:02:54.576 --> 00:02:58.129
about business in town, and
connect with them one by one

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:01.333
via coffee, via Skype, via phone call

00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:04.618
as much face to face as possible,

00:03:04.618 --> 00:03:08.019
and ask them to reverse
engineer their objectives,

00:03:08.019 --> 00:03:10.956
meaning what can the Chamber do for you?

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:13.022
What do you want out of it?

00:03:13.022 --> 00:03:15.275
I'd also have a better
understanding of what I was

00:03:15.275 --> 00:03:17.933
trying to get out of it
if I was the CEO of that.

00:03:17.933 --> 00:03:19.638
So, I don't know if that's fees,

00:03:19.638 --> 00:03:23.540
I don't know if it's something
as simply noble as making

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.867
business better in town, if
that's the objective at hand.

00:03:27.975 --> 00:03:29.856
That's a little bit of a tongue in cheek

00:03:29.856 --> 00:03:31.398
for the people that don't get my humor.

00:03:31.398 --> 00:03:33.211
I think I get razzed a
little bit too much for this.

00:03:33.211 --> 00:03:36.298
I was reading plenty of
comments on these three weeks.

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.722
Basically my job would be to make the

00:03:40.722 --> 00:03:43.542
business environment in
this community better,

00:03:43.542 --> 00:03:45.598
and I think the number
one way to do that is

00:03:45.598 --> 00:03:46.782
to get people aligned.

00:03:46.782 --> 00:03:49.707
I think leadership comes
from getting entire group of

00:03:49.707 --> 00:03:51.658
people aligned on a mission.

00:03:51.658 --> 00:03:54.664
I actually think the most
effective way to do that is

00:03:54.664 --> 00:03:57.079
to actually understand
each individual person's

00:03:57.079 --> 00:04:00.816
goals and objectives and
then come and find that

00:04:00.816 --> 00:04:03.197
little sweet spot that
is the closest thing

00:04:03.197 --> 00:04:05.101
to the overall masses that brings value

00:04:05.101 --> 00:04:06.877
across the board, and then go backwards.

00:04:06.877 --> 00:04:09.501
What's the number one thing
that I can do that brings

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.358
value to all 600 people at Vaynermedia?

00:04:11.358 --> 00:04:13.181
That brings value to all 12,000 members,

00:04:13.181 --> 00:04:15.444
and then go down the
list to where the number

00:04:15.444 --> 00:04:18.555
10 thing maybe brings value
to half of the people,

00:04:18.555 --> 00:04:20.622
but it's still better
than to three people.

00:04:20.622 --> 00:04:23.362
So, I reverse engineer
by listening upfront,

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:25.997
collecting the data, and
then executing against

00:04:25.997 --> 00:04:28.654
the top 10 things that will
bring value to everybody

00:04:28.654 --> 00:04:30.750
in the organization.

